e recipient. The internal entry gives both locators.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 66b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_66b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 69a:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_69a.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2658:1","target":{"entry":2658,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Beitzah names Rava bar Rav Huna Zuti, with Rashi’s gloss “my colleague.” Megillah names the main Rav Huna as short. Bava Batra has “to Nehardea” in the correspondence, while Ketubot reads “from Nehardea” after the recipient. Speculation about two individuals remains.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
